{"id": "EUVD-2026-58548", "enisaUuid": "33977c6b-9790-3eb2-a95b-6e6073851b52", "description": "OpenWrt LuCI contains an overly permissive ACL definition in luci-mod-system-mounts that grants write access to /etc/crontabs/root to users intended only for mount configuration. Authenticated users with only the mount-configuration ACL group can append arbitrary cron entries via ubus file.write, which the default busybox crond daemon executes as root within one minute.", "datePublished": "2026-08-13T21:54:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-30T17:20:23", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/openwrt/luci/security/advisories/GHSA-v5f9-62c7-cw29", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openwrt-luci-luci-mod-system-mounts-acl-root-rce-via-crontab-write"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6vfc-74mf-qrmj", "CVE-2026-72840"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "92a90506-dcf6-3df3-bfe3-d217bfc09536", "product": {"name": "luci", "vendor": {"name": "OpenWRT"}}, "product_version": "25.12.0 \u226425.12.5"}, {"id": "e06d9779-40a0-3269-9f95-6729b1dcb409", "product": {"name": "luci", "vendor": {"name": "OpenWRT"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226424.10.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "13157c5a-f062-3465-9f5d-a1786e772bf5", "vendor": {"name": "OpenWRT"}}], "isExploited": false}